  "query_preview": "..\n\nWEATHER PATTERN OVERVIEW:\n\nAn upper ridge over the western states will build into Montana\nthis week with temperatures warming into Friday. Look for highs \nFriday to reach the 90s north to the low 100s south. West winds \nwill also increase as a surface low passes east to the northeast \nof us. If fuels dry out enough, there could be Fire Weather \nconcerns.\n\nSomewhat lighter winds are expected Saturday but slightly lower\nhumidities will keep the Fire Weather concerns alive.\n\nSlightly cooler conditions are expected Sunday but not enough to\nremove the Fire Weather concerns. \n\nLighter winds and higher humidity, especially in the northeast\nzones should continue to hack away at the Fire Weather concerns\nMonday.\n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS:\nGoing NBM forecast generally good. Concerned that increasing smoke\naloft could suppress temperatures through the week. While have not\nadjusted temperatures, have begun to add haze into the forecast.",
